s_cec8b4967e8a673125f9313710a39939df91d337c8430aac391a45810a8c2cce: "«interface»\nDocumentSources" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "read(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "localPath(uri, manifestFile)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nDocumentSources.read:\nReturn the current saved text with this exact URI, or absence when unavailable. Do not discover projects, install dependencies or substitute empty text. Unexpected acquisition errors surface. Core overrides this saved snapshot with an open document's unsaved text.\n\nDocumentSources.localPath:\nReturn the verified portable source path relative to this selected manifest's directory, using the exact supplied source URI and native root/file ancestry facts. A named unsaved file under verified existing ancestors can have a path without reading or creating its contents. A foreign route, unsupported URI, unavailable root or route escaping the verified root has no local path; never strip a URI prefix or guess ownership from declarations, folders, generated destinations or build.sourceRoots. A nested source root cannot shorten the primary manifest-relative path. Core supplies its exact captured sourceId separately. Unexpected provider errors surface. This query does not scan, install, capture a connected project or write.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI4YzVmMGEwMy0yZTBjLTRjNDItOGU3YS03YmFiNzNjYzgzNzIiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IkRvY3VtZW50RmVlZGJhY2siLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_b56bfd6f07bd5ea3b6a48016ef49d0a86ed88472899a5643905346a4c0d35265: "«interface»\nDocumentFeedback" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "publish(source, version, report)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "clear(uri)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nDocumentFeedback.publish:\nEvery DocumentAnalysis publication includes detached immutable requirements and dependencyProblems lists prepared through the public requirementsFor and ConfigurationReader. Keep the compiler Compilation unchanged; configuration and source-ownership findings retain their actual dependency origins separately. Output-profile findings unknown-output and invalid-output-options with their actual manifest outputs origins belong to the consumer's actual output registry and are excluded from dependencyProblems; no validated package catalog or scope rows are recovered from that rejected configuration. Empty lists mean no effective scoped obligations or findings, not proof of installation. The additive optional report fields support older supplied-report consumers; this analysis always supplies both. Caller mutation cannot change an earlier or current report.\nPublish the report for this exact immutable snapshot and version. Preserve actual reader diagnostics and the complete compiler result, including nonlocated problems and deferred requirements. Compilation is absent for rejected entry syntax. Inspection is absent for rejected entry syntax; otherwise it is a public QueryInspection over the same SourceComposer Resolution.model passed to Compiler, captured once without another resolution pass. It preserves bound, invalid and deferred reference facts even when Compilation has problems or no Specification. Never retain an older Inspection after rejection. Sources are the captured texts used for located findings; dependencies are exact source URIs requested, including unavailable imports. An empty diagnostic result replaces previous problems; absence of problems alone does not establish compilation success.\nRetain that exact immutable SourceComposer Resolution in this report, captured once and passed to Compiler and the same QueryInspection before publication. Resolution is absent for rejected entry syntax; never retain an earlier accepted resolution after rejection. Current independently bound facts remain usable despite unrelated compiler problems or absent Specification. Completion consumes this same core evidence without another resolution pass; no Resolution or model crosses the native protocol boundary.\n\nDocumentFeedback.clear:\nRemove all diagnostic feedback for this exact document URI.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIzNjgyYTA5MS1lMDI1LTQyMjYtYjZmNy1hNzQ2ZTljNDUxZWQiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkRvY3VtZW50QW5hbHlzaXMiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_4804a76e9d5f0d3a98798298a60156318bcd8b1d0c2ccedd5f33698f5035d5fa: "«component»\nDocumentAnalysis" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(feedback, sources)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "opened(source, version)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "changed(source, version)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "closed(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "sourceChanged(uri)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nDocumentAnalysis.configurationChanged:\nReceive the current selected saved configuration snapshot or absence. Validate its supplied text through the public ConfigurationReader with shipped output profiles, then capture only validated Configuration.packages aliases and phases as the existing SourceComposer's DependencyPackage inputs. Missing text, invalid configuration, switching manifests or withdrawing selection replaces the prior catalog; never retain old supplied packages after an invalid or absent snapshot. Do not use writable as package availability or read unsaved configuration buffers; ConnectionSidebar supplies its actual saved-text policy. These are supplied compiler configuration facts, not proof of package installation, native exports, external declaration models, runtime behavior or generation readiness. Keep genuinely unsupplied aliases and missing phases as the language's actual findings. Do not infer packages from imports, folder names, node_modules or another project.\nA changed catalog invalidates current open analyses and republishes their exact retained unsaved sources at unchanged editor versions through the same SourceComposer, Compiler and Inspection/Resolution publication. Reuse unchanged parsed sources and saved dependency snapshots. Retain the validated catalog for ordinary source edits rather than revalidating configuration per edit. Preserve current document lifetimes and guard reentrant source/configuration/feedback changes so older work cannot publish with an obsolete catalog. Validation or publication exceptions surface; they are not empty success. Existing configuration consumers retain actual validation explanations. This operation never acquires project/package code, scans, installs, generates, saves or writes; it does not require connected-target verification.\nRetain the validated requirements metadata with the same catalog, and include the selected manifest filename and effective scope metadata in configuration currentness even when aliases/phases are unchanged. Prepare requirementsFor over the actual captured workspace source identities and provider-supplied local paths; no resolver, synthetic model or implicit runtime imports are added. Project obligations apply to supplied workspace sources even when a foreign or untitled source has no local path; folder/exact-file obligations require verified local paths. Do not treat acquired external declaration models as workspace sources. Invalid or absent configuration withdraws earlier rows/catalog and publishes the actual configuration findings; failed scope preparation publishes no old rows. A relevant saved scope change rechecks retained unsaved text at the same editor version. Cache source ownership between text edits; invalidate it after a selected configuration change or relevant source-route notification, guard reentrant provider/feedback callbacks, and never run SourceLoader or connected native capture on each keystroke.\n\nDocumentAnalysis.opened:\nStart an open document lifetime from this exact supplied snapshot. Use one retained LangiumReader and Compiler; compose accepted source models through the existing SourceComposer. Resolve authored source locators relative to their owner URI and obtain only required source snapshots through DocumentSources. Absolute URIs remain usable; a relative locator without a hierarchical owner, including untitled, remains an unavailable-module finding without guessing a workspace or throwing a URL-base error. Open unsaved text overrides saved text. Cache parsing by exact text, including rejected text; never reuse a previous accepted model after invalid edits. Publish real syntax and compiler findings without generating, installing packages or requiring a project connection. No runtime package facts are invented; unavailable prerequisites remain explicit. Treat URIs as identity. Reject invalid noninteger or negative versions with RangeError before changing state.\n\nDocumentAnalysis.changed:\nReject a noninteger or negative version with a RangeError before changing state. For an open document, check and publish only a strictly newer version. Ignore duplicate, older and unopened-document changes. Retain the exact snapshot and version for publication. Update affected open dependents as well. Check that the same lifetime, version and dependency revision remain current before publishing after reentrant source or feedback callbacks. The native caller excludes callbacks from an earlier document lifetime; URI/version alone cannot distinguish those after reopening. Syntax acceptance makes no semantic validity claim; retain compiler problems and deferred requirements. Reader or publication exceptions must surface rather than masquerade as an empty successful result.\n\nDocumentAnalysis.closed:\nEnd this open lifetime and clear its diagnostics. Ignore later changes until the document is opened again; reopening may start with a lower version. Repeated close is harmless. Imported closed documents fall back to current saved text, and affected open dependents are rechecked. Unrelated documents remain unchanged.\n\nDocumentAnalysis.sourceChanged:\nInvalidate a requested saved source after creation, change or deletion and recheck affected open entries even when their editor version is unchanged. Ignore unrelated URIs and saved changes hidden by an authoritative open snapshot. Reuse unchanged parsed snapshots and read only the invalidated source plus newly required imports. Track missing imports too, and terminate cyclic import acquisition. Preserve other documents and previous reports; do not let reentrant older work replace current feedback.\nWhen folder/file scopes are in use, a relevant file-route notification also invalidates the cached local-path fact, including for authoritative open unsaved text. Recheck the same retained snapshot if its effective scope ownership changed; do not replace that text with saved bytes. Include actually queried ownership URIs in dependencies so the existing native watch boundary can invalidate them. Unrelated notifications cannot trigger a scan or reset another document's facts.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJmZGYyNmYwYy1lOGZmLTQ5MmYtOTg0NC1mYzc5ZWJiMTQ5YzIiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkRvY3VtZW50T3V0bGluZSIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_4458458f3c3d476bd36248c4386014a50120e713e2b1c4ad867bf73f9c7ea4f6: "«component»\nDocumentOutline" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjU0MWZmNDFlLTM3NWUtNDU5Yi1iZjk1LTQ0ZTBmOTkxZDhhNyIsIm93bmVyIjoic180NDU4NDU4ZjNjM2Q0NzZiZDM2MjQ4YzQzODYwMTRhNTAxMjBlNzEzZTJiMWM0YWQ4NjdiZjczZjljN2VhNGY2IiwibmFtZSI6ImNvbnN0cnVjdGlvbiIsInBhcmFtZXRlcnMiOltdfQ
  "construction()": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "published(source, version, report)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "closed(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "symbols(uri, version)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjgyOWE4MmE4LTAwNWUtNDc2Yy04MTAyLThlM2Y2MmFlNjYxOSIsIm93bmVyIjoic180NDU4NDU4ZjNjM2Q0NzZiZDM2MjQ4YzQzODYwMTRhNTAxMjBlNzEzZTJiMWM0YWQ4NjdiZjczZjljN2VhNGY2IiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nDocumentOutline.published:\nReceive current immutable DocumentAnalysis publications from the same live analysis, including replacements at the same editor version after dependency changes. Reject noninteger or negative versions with RangeError before changing state. Prepare the current document's ordered declaration tree once from that report's public Inspection and exact captured source. This is authored structure, not a checked Specification or a claim that every reference resolves. Independent compiler problems or deferred requirements do not suppress supported declarations. Rejected entry syntax or missing exact captured text withdraws the old outline. Never parse, resolve, compile, discover files, read saved text or substitute an older accepted report here.\nInclude only source-authored component, concept, class, interface, record-type-declaration, alias-type-declaration, opaque-type-declaration, field, function and capability items belonging to this exact source URI. Names are the public decoded names; kind is exactly the listed language kind. Use each item's actual finite source origin and nameOrigin, requiring the nonempty name selection to be contained in the whole declaration and both ranges to fit the captured text. Preserve source order and actual public parent/children containment. Omit local wrappers while retaining their supported declarations beneath the nearest supported enclosing declaration. Do not emit import/public references, parameters, helpers, examples, scenario/interaction support, external or builtin nodes; do not promote declarations from excluded example/helper bodies. Do not infer nesting from spelling, references or dependencies. Imported declarations never become this document's outline.\nEach emitted child's whole range must also be contained in its emitted parent's whole range. Omit an invalid supported declaration and its subtree rather than invent ranges or promote its children into a different parent.\n\nDocumentOutline.closed:\nForget this exact document's outline when DocumentAnalysis ends its lifetime. Repeated close is harmless and other documents remain usable. A later current publication after reopening starts a new lifetime and may have a lower version.\n\nDocumentOutline.symbols:\nReject a noninteger or negative version with RangeError before changing state. Return the prepared outline only for the exact retained URI/version and current captured text. A current accepted document with no supported declarations has an empty symbols list. Missing, stale, rejected, closed or disposed publications return absence. The reply includes the exact captured source used for all whole/name scalar ranges. A request performs no Inspection walk, parsing, checking, acquisition, generation or project scan. Caller mutation cannot change retained state or other earlier/current replies; use immutable values or independent copies. This operation never writes files or changes editor selection.\n\nDocumentOutline.dispose:\nEnd this outline lifetime, clear retained trees and ignore later publications. All queries return absence; repeated disposal is harmless.\n```"
}
