  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjJkMWI0MTUwLWNhM2MtNGY0OS05MWM1LWE0YzBmYzk4ZWFkOCIsIm93bmVyIjoic181ODY3ZmQxMGE5NTlmZGJmMGE4NjA4NDc2ZjNhMTA4YTI4ZDRjNjI0YWY4MzQ1YTNlYzIyNTQzZmM5ZDliNWM1IiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nGenerationOnSave.configurationChanged:\nCapture the selected saved manifest and its explicit opt-in. Absence or a different filename withdraws the prior lifetime; enabled never transfers to another manifest. Missing opt-in means disabled, independently of writable or connected status. Changed selection/text/enablement cancels obsolete work and clears its queue. Never rewrite configuration, install or build merely because configuration or enablement changed.\n\nGenerationOnSave.sourceSaved:\nReject a nonpositive or noninteger version with RangeError before changing state. Capture this actual local .expec post-save snapshot. Reject a missing/disabled connection, mismatched actual saved source/configuration bytes or a different current clean buffer, with an explanation and no new worker. Validate through the real registered ConfigurationReader, resolving entries from its actual manifest source URI. A save must belong to an actual configured entry or its saved import closure, established through real saved-source acquisition, public LangiumReader models and SourceComposer composition, not source-name guessing or a single-entry DocumentReport. An unrelated .expec save creates no build. The SDK full build owns remaining prerequisites and invalid compilation findings. Present built only for an actual successful complete build result; preserve actual refused/failed/cancelled findings and partial receipts. Superseded results are recorded but cannot replace current state. Start at most one full saved build for this connection. While it runs, keep only the latest save, cancel the obsolete run and wait for its settlement before starting that latest request after fresh checks. Repeated later saves can retry at the same editor version. Never feed a selected DocumentReport as a full build.\n\nGenerationOnSave.editorChanged:\nInspect fresh GenerationFiles facts. An edit/close of the triggering source, dirty selected manifest, any observed dirty .expec buffer or dirty ordinary buffer within the actual SDK target root invalidates the pending save and requests cancellation. Logical/canonical root aliases are checked conservatively; uncertain classification is an explained refusal. Unrelated buffer changes create no build. Only sourceSaved creates a generation intent; generated filesystem notifications still reach existing analysis/writer freshness checks without becoming new save intents or being globally muted. Each SDK permission query rechecks current facts.\n\nGenerationOnSave.dispose:\nEnd this lifetime, clear queued saves and request cancellation once. Start no later work or current-state publication; retain actual terminal effect records. Native ownership uses GenerationWorker.dispose completion to await worker/process cleanup and keep effect recording alive until settlement. No synchronous termination or automatic rollback is promised.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJjYTA3ODJjOC02MmMyLTQ5YTYtOTZhYi04M2Q2YTRiMTE4N2UiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IlByZXZpZXdGZWVkYmFjayIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_d8e3b80ce06d1586b655ff123ac5dab526edefe4856f2c87c27992c64f01cee3: "«interface»\nPreviewFeedback" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "present(publication)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nPreviewFeedback.present:\nPresent this complete plain-data view in order. URI/version identify its authored source for the title and observations. Tabs have unique configured IDs, labels, status, ordered UTF-8 documents and any actual explanation. Whole-view message explains absent/invalid configuration or selection. Optional blocked is true only for an actual rejected configuration; it gives the UI a truthful whole-view blocked presentation while all old tabs/documents remain withdrawn. Absence of tabs or a general message is not proof of failure. This accepted view is authoritative; host/UI adapters do not compare report revisions or implement another freshness policy. Keep the latest complete accepted presentation for native ready replay. No model, Specification, native buffer, function or Error crosses transport.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJhNWEyNzk5Zi00OWE2LTQ1MGEtYjY3OC04YzE5M2RlNWE2MGMiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IlByZXZpZXdDb25maWd1cmF0aW9uRmVlZGJhY2siLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_2ac9804244842bc553a1d0ea14249dd1d90fddbb6b72ae6a50a8ab264cde6805: "«interface»\nPreviewConfigurationFeedback" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nPreviewConfigurationFeedback.configurationChanged:\nForward the current selected saved manifest snapshot or absence, preserving its absolute filename/text and selection lifetime. Dirty manifest editing retains its saved snapshot policy. Switching away from a selected local manifest withdraws the prior snapshot. This event grants no permission to write, capture targets or claim connection/generation readiness.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIxZjM5MjcyZi1lM2Q1LTQ1M2YtYmZhZS02YmJkZTViMDgxOTkiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6Ik91dHB1dFByZXZpZXdzIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_4dfa45e16e865bb5830aa68ffa99b721888a6d4596b71caaec81bb7ae49aa680: "«component»\nOutputPreviews" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(feedback, registrations)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "selected(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "published(source, version, report)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "closed(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjMyMDZlNWZhLWUyZTQtNDdkMi04Y2NlLWNjMWMzZmYyN2M2YiIsIm93bmVyIjoic180ZGZhNDVlMTZlODY1YmI1ODMwYWE2OGZmYTk5YjcyMTg4OGE2ZDQ1OTZiNzFjYWFlYzgxYmI3YWU0OWFhNjgwIiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nOutputPreviews.configurationChanged:\nCapture this current saved manifest or absence and advance private currentness before further work. Prepare the real Outputs registry and ConfigurationReader from supplied registrations, or shipped built-ins when absent. An explicit list replaces built-ins. Validate through ConfigurationReader without discovering files. Missing/invalid configuration withdraws old tabs with its actual explanation. An actual rejected ConfigurationReader result also publishes whole-view blocked true; selection absence, waiting and an empty configured output set do not invent that failure marker. Preserve configured output IDs/order/options; duplicate IDs remain a configuration error. Changed options replace queued requests. Valid outputs may preview without a project or with an unavailable target; target availability is not authored-preview readiness. Use this absolute native manifest filename as OutputContext.manifestLocation. Do not install, capture targets, rewrite configuration or request generation.\n\nOutputPreviews.selected:\nSelect the exact authored document URI or absence, advancing private currentness. Retain current reports for open documents so switching selections requires no recompile. A selected document without a current report has a visible waiting explanation. A preview panel taking focus is not a new authored selection. Selection replaces queued requests and cannot let a previous document's completion restore old content.\n\nOutputPreviews.published:\nActual dependencyProblems in this current report block configured outputs with their real codes/messages and dependency-origin paths, withdrawing old documents even when editor version is unchanged. Do not manufacture a compiler failure or ignore an invalid scoped configuration merely because the unchanged source's Compilation has a Specification. Successful scoped requirements permit ordinary previews using the same checked source; they do not install packages, capture a target or prove native generation readiness. Legacy supplied reports without this additive field have no extra scope findings.\nReceive the real current immutable DocumentAnalysis publication before native diagnostic conversion loses its Compilation. Keep the source/version and complete report inside core; never parse, compile, discover files or rebuild models here. Each publication is a new private report revision even at the same editor version after imported-source changes. Only the selected current report drives previews. Rejected syntax or absent/failed/deferred Compilation blocks configured tabs with actual syntax/compiler codes/messages or requirement reasons/requires and no old documents. From its checked Specification call public Outputs.preview independently for each configured ID/options with captured report source URIs as workspaceModules and the selected manifest filename. Publish pending tabs with no previous documents before starting work; each current completion updates only its tab while others progress. Retain actual document paths/media types/order and optional validated SVG diagram annotations, including exact renderer image coordinates, capability identity/label and authored promise strings. Copy annotations as plain data without source parsing or native handles. Strictly decode supported UTF-8 text media, application/json and image/svg+xml from their exact byte spans; invalid UTF-8 or unsupported binary presentation refuses that output with an explicit unsupported-presentation explanation and no silent replacement. Successful empty documents are ready with No authored documents; refused checks retain actual diagnostic codes/messages or requirement reasons/requires. Provider/contract exceptions are visibly refused rather than fabricated upstream findings or empty success. Status is pending, ready, blocked or refused. Private work currentness covers source lifetime/version, report/configuration/selection revisions and coordinator lifetime; check it after every await and discard stale success/refusal/error. Keep at most one invocation per output ID in flight and only its latest requested report/configuration queued; after settlement render that latest request and skip superseded intermediate edits. Other IDs progress independently. Do not open project adapters, capture a target, plan/apply writes, generate acceptance output, execute scenarios or claim handwritten preservation/write readiness.\n\nOutputPreviews.closed:\nForget this open report lifetime, clear selection if it owns the selected source, invalidate pending work and clear queued requests for it. Later old completions cannot publish. Reopening the same URI may start at a lower version and is a distinct report lifetime. Other retained open reports remain usable.\n\nOutputPreviews.dispose:\nEnd this coordinator lifetime, clear retained reports/queued work and prevent new invocations or later publication. Repeated disposal is harmless. Already started callbacks have rejection handlers and settle through their own cleanup; this operation does not claim synchronous worker termination. Real UML callbacks own one engine per invocation, reuse it across documents and dispose before settlement.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIyZmU5YTllYy1jNmUwLTRjZmEtYWYzOC05MmQxYmFlNjQ2Y2QiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IkNvbm5lY3Rpb25Xb3JrRmVlZGJhY2siLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_172c4f66624a2211a5dd0c4dd4bea9a6049f7cd6c39f664440bb0e45138b77ef: "«interface»\nConnectionWorkFeedback" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nConnectionWorkFeedback.configurationChanged:\nReceive an immutable captured saved configuration only for this controller's current connected selection, or absence when checking a different target, disconnected, deleting metadata, unavailable, invalid, unconfigured or disposed. This controls connection-owned work, independently of authored preview configuration. Absence cancels existing generation admission and clears queued save intents through the existing GenerationHost; it does not erase prior explicit per-manifest opt-in or discard terminal results and partial receipts. Receiving configuration is not a save intent and never starts generation. Preview and live-analysis consumers continue receiving the selected saved metadata through their existing independent boundary.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI3MGU0ZjVlMC1mOTY0LTQ3MDktYmI2Ni0zZmNhZDMwNjc3N2YiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IkNvbm5lY3Rpb25GZWVkYmFjayIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_6741902b4e1b29ab7fab5c953c44c780536f6f068b11fbafb9a56ae60bf2df03: "«interface»\nConnectionFeedback" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "present(state)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "saveConfiguration(previous, text)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nConnectionFeedback.present:\nPresent this immutable current state. Status is unconfigured, checking, connected, disconnected, unavailable or invalid. Target is the absolute logical configured or currently requested directory. verifiedDirectory is the actual canonical directory from the existing connector, only while connected. Connected establishes valid configuration and usable filesystem identity; it does not establish native build or dependency readiness. Disconnected means an explicit session-only suspension; saved metadata and target files remain intact.\n\nConnectionFeedback.saveConfiguration:\nRequest conditional persistence for this exact captured previous snapshot. This request is not a completed save. Preserve dirty editor work and refuse if actual saved bytes or write safety no longer match previous. Confirm success with the actual saved configurationChanged snapshot, or return this same previous object to saveFailed.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI4MWViOWE4Mi04NTY0LTRmYjAtOWQyMS04NTE4ZWM4ZDI3M2MiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkNvbm5lY3Rpb25Db250cm9sbGVyIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_3d3959c32ca1a983b602b3bbc3f9d83649e800407059e470ff0bac048b2172eb: "«component»\nConnectionController" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(feedback)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "observeWork(feedback)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjYxYzljZjUyLWZmZTYtNGM4OS1hOWFkLWEwYjFjZTMzNTI2OSIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZDM5NTljMzJjYTFhOTgzYjYwMmIzYmJjM2Y5ZDgzNjQ5ZTgwMDQwNzA1OWU0NzBmZjBiYWMwNDhiMjE3MmViIiwibmFtZSI6Imd1aWRhbmNlIiwicGFyYW1ldGVycyI6W119
  "guidance()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(snapshot)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "chooseProject(directory)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "createConnection(directory, outputs, entries)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjFlNzlkMzEwLTk0ODEtNGUzMi05NWE5LWU0M2FlMzMzZWQyMyIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZDM5NTljMzJjYTFhOTgzYjYwMmIzYmJjM2Y5ZDgzNjQ5ZTgwMDQwNzA1OWU0NzBmZjBiYWMwNDhiMjE3MmViIiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc2Nvbm5lY3QiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "disconnect()": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImI0MDdlMDc4LWQ3ZmMtNDBjNi1hNzE4LTBmNDY5M2YxMWI0YiIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZDM5NTljMzJjYTFhOTgzYjYwMmIzYmJjM2Y5ZDgzNjQ5ZTgwMDQwNzA1OWU0NzBmZjBiYWMwNDhiMjE3MmViIiwibmFtZSI6InJlY29ubmVjdCIsInBhcmFtZXRlcnMiOltdfQ
  "reconnect()": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImYzZmQ0ODZhLTMwY2QtNGE4Zi04NTRiLTU2MDQzNDA5OWNlZSIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZDM5NTljMzJjYTFhOTgzYjYwMmIzYmJjM2Y5ZDgzNjQ5ZTgwMDQwNzA1OWU0NzBmZjBiYWMwNDhiMjE3MmViIiwibmFtZSI6ImRlbGV0ZUNvbm5lY3Rpb24iLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "deleteConnection()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "targetChanged(path)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "saveFailed(previous, message)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjAwOTY1OGFmLWZmM2EtNGU1Ny04ZTI1LWVkNmQ4MGE4MmQxNiIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZDM5NTljMzJjYTFhOTgzYjYwMmIzYmJjM2Y5ZDgzNjQ5ZTgwMDQwNzA1OWU0NzBmZjBiYWMwNDhiMjE3MmViIiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nConnectionController.observeWork:\nAttach one replaceable work observer without changing this controller's constructor or requiring metadata-only callers to attach one. Immediately deliver the current active saved snapshot or absence. Replacing an observer withdraws the previous observer first; disposal withdraws and releases it. Capture observer identity and controller revision around every callback. Reentrant replacement, disconnect, configuration changes or disposal cannot subsequently deliver old active work or overwrite newer state. Host callback failures remain observable; do not swallow them or skip owned cleanup. The actual extension assembly attaches its one existing GenerationHost through this operation, rather than routing generation through preview feedback.\n\nConnectionController.guidance:\nReturn synchronous detached immutable facts prepared from the current captured saved snapshot and its already validated configuration. Missing metadata has requiresEntries true and hasProject false. Existing valid metadata keeps its build, has requiresEntries false and hasProject exactly when its validated project exists. A requested unsaved target is not saved project metadata. Invalid metadata, no captured selection or a disposed lifetime returns absence. List configured outputs first in actual authored order with configured true and no suggestedDirectory, then eligible new typescript, uml and markdown IDs not already configured with configured false and suggestions '.', 'diagrams' and 'docs'. Suggestions are core-owned extension setup policy, not SDK defaults. Do not expose or reconstruct retained options; createConnection preserves their actual saved values. Return file, exact text or absence, and writable from the same captured snapshot, including dirty write safety. Caller mutation cannot alter earlier or future facts. Prepare facts when the saved configuration changes; this query performs no parsing, validation, connector work, reads, state publication, observer notification or persistence. It does not change session suspension or generation opt-in.\n\nConnectionController.configurationChanged:\nCapture this exact saved text and write safety for one selected local manifest. Advance currentness before any asynchronous work and withdraw the old connected state while checking. Missing text is unconfigured. Validate existing text with the real ConfigurationReader and registered built-in output profiles; invalid configuration stays invalid with its real diagnostic message and is never rewritten. Use ProjectConnector.connect with this absolute manifest filename. A valid configuration without a project is unconfigured; an unavailable root is unavailable; only an actual connected result establishes connected and verifiedDirectory. Preserve logical target and canonical verified directory separately. An explicit disconnect remains suspended across saved changes to this same manifest and target events; selecting a different manifest starts its own unsuspended selection. Forward current active work only through the attached work observer, with absence before obsolete work can continue. Do not scan or capture a project, install packages, generate outputs or parse native project code. Only the latest configuration/target revision may publish.\n\nConnectionController.chooseProject:\nChoose an absolute native directory for the current selected configuration. Reject invalid existing configuration without rewriting it. If writable is false, preserve the current target, request no save and present the message Save or revert unsaved configuration edits before choosing a project. Verify the proposed directory through the real connector before requesting persistence. A missing or unusable directory remains unavailable and requests no save. Preserve every other existing JSON field, including project.excludePaths; change only project.root. For a missing manifest, propose formatVersion 1, version 0.1.0, build.entries [src/main.expec] and outputs []. This is this extension's explicit initial metadata setting, not a language default; connection does not check whether that source file exists, and authors must configure their actual build entry before compilation, with the selected root. Never write the file itself or report the new project connected before actual saved confirmation. Pass an immutable captured previous snapshot to feedback. New configuration or target revisions invalidate older verification and any unsent write request.\n\nConnectionController.createConnection:\nRetain existing project settings, including project.excludePaths; change only project.root within that object. Create or replace this selected manifest's project connection using an actual absolute target directory and the author's ordered output choices. Validate before requesting a conditional save; unknown or repeated IDs, unsupported new profiles, invalid relative destinations, invalid existing configuration, dirty write safety or missing required entries request no persistence. Preserve existing version, build including entries, packages, libraries and all other metadata. For each selected already configured ID retain its exact options; do not normalize, flatten or replace advanced settings. A retained choice omits directory or supplies its unchanged existing destination; a different destination requires editing the manifest. Removing an ID removes only its output configuration, never target artifacts. Newly selected profiles are limited to typescript, uml and markdown and require a nonblank destination relative to the target. Validate the complete proposal using actual shipped ConfigurationReader profiles. New TypeScript options are sourceRoot '.', directory the supplied value and no configFile, preserving folders relative to this manifest's source folder; '.' is a usable target-root destination, not an SDK default. New UML options are directory plus views ['structure']; new Markdown options contain directory. The native guide's suggested destinations are author choices, not language defaults. For missing text require an explicitly supplied nonempty list of literal relative source entries; propose formatVersion 1 and version 0.1.0 with those actual entries. Never discover sources, assume src/main.expec exists, scaffold a target, install packages or claim generation readiness. Existing metadata does not need new entries and retains its build unchanged. Verify the proposed target with the real connector; both empty and existing usable directories can connect. Invalidate older verification, pending saves and connection-owned work before accepting a new target. Request only manifest persistence through feedback with the exact captured previous snapshot, and remain checking until actual saved confirmation. A successful explicit creation resumes this session's selection. No target or authored-source writes.\n\nConnectionController.disconnect:\nSuspend this selected connection for this session only. Invalidate verification and unsent persistence, withdraw connection-owned work before presenting disconnected with the saved logical target and no verifiedDirectory. A missing project remains unconfigured. Preserve every saved manifest byte, output/package setting and target file. Explain that reconnection is available and the suspension is not persisted. Relevant target restoration or same-manifest saved changes do not silently reconnect. Keep independent authored previews and live package configuration available; no automatic generation or rollback claim.\n\nConnectionController.reconnect:\nResume this session's selection by freshly validating the latest captured saved metadata and checking its current target through the real connector. Withdraw old work until actual current verification succeeds. Unavailable, invalid or missing metadata stays honest and requests no save. Preserve saved configuration, previous explicit per-manifest generation opt-in and target files; previously disabled stays disabled. Reconnection neither grants opt-in nor replays a save intent: even an earlier true opt-in requires a subsequent genuine source save before any generation. Only the current reconnect revision can present or activate work.\n\nConnectionController.deleteConnection:\nRemove only this selected saved manifest's project metadata through the same conditional persistence feedback. Reject invalid or dirty configuration without rewriting it, and treat an already absent project as unconfigured without a write. Preserve version, build, outputs, packages, libraries and all other fields exactly as values; never delete the manifest, target directory, generated files or handwritten files. Invalidate pending verification and withdraw connection-owned work before requesting removal. A request is not deletion success; become unconfigured only after actual saved confirmation without project. Failures use the exact pending previous snapshot and remain observable. Authored output previews still receive the saved retained output configuration.\n\nConnectionController.targetChanged:\nRecheck the current configured target automatically after relevant logical or canonical root or ancestor events, including deletion and restoration. Ignore unrelated paths and events for a superseded target, and never resume an explicitly disconnected session from watcher events. Reuse validated current configuration; perform only connector identity/availability checking, not tree capture. Withdraw connected while rechecking and suppress stale completion.\n\nConnectionController.saveFailed:\nFor the exact previous object of the current pending save request, report unavailable with this host failure message; never pretend the requested configuration was saved or connected. Ignore failures from superseded requests.\n\nConnectionController.dispose:\nEnd this controller lifetime, invalidate pending asynchronous work and prevent later publication or save requests. Withdraw and release the attached work observer even if another cleanup callback fails. Repeated disposal is harmless; the native caller owns watchers and view registrations.\n```"
}
