  "configuration()": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjE0YzRjMjYxLTUwY2MtNDkwOC1iNTZlLTM0MDJkOTMwOTYzZSIsIm93bmVyIjoic182ZmZlMDg4OWJhY2QzZjE4MzEwOWZhM2I2ZGRmY2U5OTM2YWY1YWY5NjdjYzhhMzM4NjZiZjY0Zjk0N2M3MWZmIiwibmFtZSI6Im9wZW5Eb2N1bWVudHMiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "openDocuments()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nRenameWorkspace.configuration:\nReturn the currently selected saved manifest snapshot, or absence. Never invent a default entry, discover a project or substitute an old selection. Use the active saved configuration, not unsaved JSON editor proposals. An unavailable selected manifest is not usable. writable is metadata-save permission and is not rename permission; this operation never edits that manifest. Returned facts are caller-isolated; they do not prove that a generated-output project is connected.\n\nRenameWorkspace.openDocuments:\nReturn a fresh complete snapshot of the current open .expec text documents, including hidden unsaved buffers, with their exact URI/text and actual nonnegative integer version. No duplicate URI or guessed saved version. Closed documents are absent. No writes, parsing, source discovery, generation or editor selection.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJhNTY2ODkyYS04YzJiLTQ1ZGMtYjhhMC1kNDNlNmY2MDY3NzQiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZUlkZW50aXRpZXMiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_0fbf70fa75b7a12f4f0849a610e9318a91a607d832723a14a876c058387c971d: "«interface»\nSourceIdentities" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "keyOf(uri, manifestFile)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceIdentities.keyOf:\nReturn the current opaque physical source identity within this selected manifest, or absence when native facts cannot establish it. Equal known keys establish the same actual file; different known keys establish different actual files in this capture. The provider owns filesystem observation and ancestry checks; core receives no native handles or filesystem APIs. Never derive a key from URI spelling, decoded or case-folded strings, localPath, source text or declaration names. Keys are only equality facts for the current capture, never persistent or cross-project identifiers. A native file that has never been saved may have no identity: preserve absence so rename can explain its actual URI and ask the author to save first. No project scan, package capture, parsing, generation or writes. Unexpected provider errors surface. Return current facts on every query so the caller can recheck all acquired and routed source identities before returning a plan.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI3ZmNmOTBkMy03ZWUzLTQ1ZTItYjc4My1mYjJmYzkxNjdkYjkiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZVJlbmFtZSIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_59d1da264bc927fb207545f213f1a60893f31f29c07b62a8798bb4632ec977a2: "«component»\nSourceRename" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(workspace, sources, identities)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "prepare(uri, version, offset)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "rename(uri, version, offset, newName)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceRename.prepare:\nCheck one explicit rename request against the selected manifest's actual build.entries and every transitive use/include/examples attachment reached from those entries, including reverse users reached from another entry. This is configured-build scope, not arbitrary workspace files or other projects. Read validated configuration through the public ConfigurationReader; a generated-output connection is not required. Use current open text before saved DocumentSources text, including new unsaved import locators. Capture each exact URI/text once per analysis and terminate cycles; never reuse an accepted model after rejected text. Ask SourceIdentities.keyOf for actual physical equality independently of DocumentSources.localPath, which remains literal requirement-scope metadata. A resolved route may use one current open buffer only when both its verified primary manifest-relative path and its known physical key agree with that buffer. Preserve the exact open URI/text/version in captured sources, models and returned edits. Refuse multiple open identities for one physical file, an equal path with different or unknown physical keys, or distinct effective acquired URIs sharing one physical key. Different paths with the same key, including native case aliases and hardlinks, refuse rather than merge requirement scopes. Unknown identities of unrelated uncaptured foreign open buffers do not match and do not block an otherwise complete rename. Never infer physical equality from URI or path spelling, case-folding, percent decoding or equal text. Use public LangiumReader, LangiumModel, SourceComposer and Compiler for one shared batch of all configured entries, with the same captured module objects and supplied package aliases/phases. Resolve configured entry paths relative to the selected manifest URI or absolute native filename, never the generated project.root. Do not create another parser or resolver. Ordinary live diagnostics and bounded references remain unchanged; only explicit prepare/rename can acquire this configured source set. Never use native project capture, SourceLoader's saved-only snapshots, package installation, JVMs, output generation or writes.\nRequire the requesting exact URI/version to be open in this captured configured scope. Require finite nonnegative integer version/offset, otherwise throw RangeError. Select the actual named source declaration or checked source-name use (including a record field label or bound final reference segment) containing the zero-based Unicode-scalar cursor; return its whole authored token range in the requesting source and decoded target name. Comments, punctuation, qualified-reference prefix segments, builtin/external/unnamed targets, unresolved/ambiguous targets and foreign source ownership refuse with an explained Error. Every acquired configured source must have a verified primary manifest-relative path from DocumentSources.localPath and a known physical key from SourceIdentities.keyOf. An unknown acquired identity refuses with the actual URI; explain save first when a new native file has no identity. A selected alias-use cursor or a same-spelled explicit alias to this target refuses rather than guessing which introduction supplied that spelling. A direct declaration or import source-name remains eligible beside a distinct explicit alias.\nRefuse incomplete or invalid checked analysis: missing required source, rejected syntax, actual compiler problems, deferred compilation prerequisites or invalid requirementsFor findings remain explained, never repaired by scanning. Use Specification.names.at, inSource and occurrencesOf for the actual checked spelling owner, not raw contextual Inspection.resolution. Require complete finding-free source-name queries even after compilation succeeds; ambiguous-source-name and source-name-selection findings refuse. Structurally empty-name captured input models need no invented query source identity. Contextual resolver deferrals already discharged by Compiler are not independent failures. Before returning, require the selected configuration and all captured open URI/text/version facts to remain equal and freshly re-read saved-only captures to match exactly. After the final saved-only rereads, requery every acquired URI and every resolved alias route that was mapped to an open buffer through SourceIdentities.keyOf using the same captured manifest; each known physical key must still agree with its captured key. Recheck current configuration and open facts after identity-provider callbacks. A changed, missing or contradictory identity refuses instead of returning an older routing plan. Explain changed input instead of returning older facts. There is no cross-call target handle: rename performs fresh capture and selection. Expected refusals use ordinary Error messages naming the actual unavailable URI, declined alias/name or changed/conflicting input; do not fabricate an empty successful edit. Unexpected provider/SDK errors surface.\n\nSourceRename.rename:\nApply prepare's same source-scope, selection, validity and final-currentness rules to fresh inputs. newName is the decoded name, not source syntax. Reject empty names, control characters and unpaired surrogates with an explained Error; do not trim or normalize Unicode or whitespace. Use the real reader to admit an ordinary single-name spelling consuming the entire candidate token; otherwise render a backtick name escaping backticks/backslashes and validate that complete token with the reader. A temporary inert synthetic source may validate spelling only: require exactly one declaration, its whole nameOrigin consuming the candidate token and its decoded name equal to newName. Reject injected trailing declarations/tokens. Never accept unchecked interpolation or use a second keyword/identifier grammar. An unchanged decoded name returns an empty edit list after validation.\nPlan the declaration name and all safely identified bound occurrences of that same declaration across the captured configured entries. Edit import source-name tokens, keeping distinct explicit aliases and their uses unchanged. Do not replace every location from bounded reference search, edit strings/comments, rename an unrelated same-named declaration, alter manifest metadata, generate files or execute a save. Same-spelled explicit alias routing refuses; selected qualifier renames and any other unproven routing refuse rather than dropping affected occurrences. Return only affected documents in URI code-unit order, each with exact captured source, its actual open version or absence for saved-only text, and distinct nonoverlapping scalar edits in descending start order. Return caller-isolated facts.\nCheck the hypothetical edited source snapshots through the same real language pipeline before returning. Clean compilation alone is insufficient: match source declarations by their mapped authored provenance/kind and every actual checked source-name token's spelling-owner declaration by mapped source/name ranges, including unchanged references that a new name could capture. Require a full two-way correspondence of complete before/after name sets: compare actual source owner kind and mapped nameOrigin (actual Name origin for aliases/captures), and stable builtin/external provenance where applicable. Unchanged tokens retain spelling/owner, while edited target-owned tokens have the decoded newName and mapped owner. Opaque NodeIds are valid only inside their own analysis and must not be compared across reparses. Refuse duplicate declarations, changed binding, lost qualified uses, new ambiguity or any new/retained prerequisite; expose the conflicting newName or actual finding. No partial plan escapes a refusal. This promises a complete intended edit against captured sources and detects supersession while computing; the ordinary editor owns later preview/apply, optional edit selection and undo. It does not promise filesystem/editor atomicity after the response.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI5NmNkYmE2OC03Nzg4LTQ0MDItYmFiMS0xYTcxNTQ4YzI0NzgiLCJraW5kIjoiaW50ZXJmYWNlIiwibmFtZSI6IlByb2plY3RPdXRwdXRzIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_e0da6d9b0a1fdec6ca7ab1f9eb3548f0dc5b26a4f5c7508bb73ccd5fc10874bf: "«interface»\nProjectOutputs" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "preview(source)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "generate(source)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nProjectOutputs.preview:\nUse the supplied document text, including unsaved edits, without writing project files. Return one tab per configured output in configuration order, retaining its registration ID and label. This established synchronous seam forwards supplied tabs; EXT-05's native live previews instead receive current DocumentReport publications through OutputPreviews, without another parser or a duplicate live pipeline.\n\nProjectOutputs.generate:\nGenerate from the supplied document through this connection's configured outputs and existing ownership and preservation rules. Never overwrite handwritten work.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJjMGFjOTIxNS02ZDFiLTQ5ODYtOTliNS0xOWRhYTA4OTk0ZDUiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IldvcmtzcGFjZUNvcmUiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_9a5426fd73f66fb45d60aa198ca6c00452d06457bb91702af27264b8d71f1df8: "«component»\nWorkspaceCore" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(outputs, generateOnSave)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "preview(source)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "sourceSaved(source)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nWorkspaceCore.preview:\nAsk the connected outputs to preview this exact document and return their tabs unchanged. Do not request generation.\n\nWorkspaceCore.sourceSaved:\nIf generateOnSave is enabled, request generation of this exact document once. Otherwise request nothing. This observes an editor save; it does not save the source file.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJmMTMxNDFlMy01NzdhLTQxNTctODY3MC04MzY4OGU1ZTM5ODUiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6Ik91dHB1dFRhYnMiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_3ca299356d77cf5fcb4b370654e20488ba4e2c2312b9c80a8e94c176ac05f44c: "«component»\nOutputTabs" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(hostElementId)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "present(tabs)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImUzZThkYzBmLTJjYjQtNDU1Zi05MTA0LTAyZTk5MzY5YmFiNiIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zY2EyOTkzNTZkNzdjZjVmY2I0YjM3MDY1NGUyMDQ4OGJhNGUyYzIzMTJiOWM4MGE4ZTk0YzE3NmFjMDVmNDRjIiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nOutputTabs.present:\nPresent exactly the supplied output IDs/labels/order, statuses, explanations and ordered document paths. Replace the previous presentation. Preserve selected output ID and document path while retained. Otherwise choose the first output, and prefer its first supplied SVG document, then its first Markdown document named Home.md, then its first document. The Home.md filename is the final slash-separated path segment; ties retain supplied order. Show pending, blocked or refused explanations without old documents; ready with no documents visibly says No authored documents.\nRender text/markdown as a readable document with headings, lists, GFM tables and fenced code. Hide HTML comments, including expec-section, expec-fragment and expec-end ownership markers. Convert only exact generated empty anchors with an expec- prefix and lowercase hexadecimal suffix into inert DOM targets; ignore all other authored HTML and attributes. Code-fenced HTML remains visible code. Never execute authored HTML or load Markdown images; show their alt text instead.\nMarkdown links resolve relative to the selected document among supplied Markdown paths within the same output. Following an available link selects that actual document path and scrolls its decoded fragment target into view; a fragment-only link stays in the current document. Never fetch a missing page or use filesystem or VS Code APIs. External, absolute, command, javascript, file and unavailable-page links remain readable and inactive with the explanation Link unavailable in supplied previews. A missing fragment visibly reports Anchor unavailable in supplied preview.\nDisplay TypeScript, JSON and other supported text literally. A D2 document initially shows Diagram preview unavailable. Select an SVG document or show source. Its explicit Show source control reveals the supplied D2 literally. Do not render Markdown, SVG or D2 source as the default document preview.\nWhen an SVG supplies diagram annotations, show a compact promise count button beside each annotated capability row; hide full promise text by default. Use renderer coordinates for the row highlight and button at every zoom level and while scrolling. Hover or keyboard focus shows the exact promises as readable plain text in an anchored thought bubble. Click or Enter pins it; clicking another indicator replaces the pinned bubble. Escape, an outside click or clicking the pinned indicator closes it. Only one bubble is visible; pointer leave or focus leave closes an unpinned bubble. The bubble stays open when its content is hovered. Keep long text wrapped and independently scrollable. Never interpret promise text as HTML or Markdown.\nThe promise state belongs only to the current image and annotations. Switching documents/outputs, replacing content or annotations, withdrawing a ready preview and disposal clear it. Show no controls for unannotated SVGs or operations without promises. Keep indicators keyboard accessible with the capability label and promise count, aria-expanded state and an accessible popup label. Escape returns to the closed state without reopening just because focus remains on the indicator.\nDisplay image/svg+xml as an inert image from its supplied UTF-8 content, never injected markup or a target-file path. Use a scroll viewport with default 100 percent scale, author-controlled zoom and reset to 100 percent; do not shrink wide images to fit. Dispose replaced image resources and bind image events to the actual content's current node. Unsupported presentation media shows a clear explanation and retains its path/type. Selection, source viewing and document navigation never compile, generate, write, fetch external resources or implement report freshness.\n\nOutputTabs.dispose:\nUnmount this view and release its handlers and owned image resources. Keep the supplied host element in the page. Repeated disposal is harmless; present after disposal reports a clear error.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIyYzczOTg3NS02M2U1LTRiNDItOTljZi02NDFjODVjNTE1NjciLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZU91dGxpbmVBZGFwdGVyIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_83bf5b4150d52848cec9e9b56cc008e1bff7a886ec339de57718bfe2c22fb6fd: "«component»\nSourceOutlineAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(outline)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "symbols(document)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceOutlineAdapter.symbols:\nAsk the one supplied DocumentOutline for this exact native document URI/version. Without a current reply whose captured URI and text exactly match document.getText(), return an empty list. Convert the reply's whole and authored-name scalar offsets to zero-based UTF-16 LSP range and selectionRange against that same captured text, retaining decoded names, source order and nested children. Require finite integer offsets, valid scalar boundaries and whole-range containment of the nonempty name selection; reject an invalid reply rather than clamp, widen or guess. Use native DocumentSymbol values only: component maps to Module, concept to Object, class to Class, interface to Interface, record-type-declaration to Struct, alias-type-declaration and opaque-type-declaration to Class, field to Field, function to Function and capability to Method. This mapping describes presentation, not a new type system. Never parse, resolve, compile, read files, generate, select targets or rebuild the tree in this adapter.\nNative DocumentSymbol names must contain nonwhitespace text. Omit a symbol with an empty or whitespace-only decoded name and its whole subtree, retaining other valid siblings in order. Never fabricate a display name or promote its children beneath a different parent. Core retains the actual decoded language facts.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI4MGQ1ZjYxOC05MWRjLTRmN2ItYjU4ZS0wY2Y3OTQ5ZjRhMTUiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkVkaXRvckFkYXB0ZXIiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_ae8e8143eb2cccb0c92560816a8416742c509cb6fcab835f778c161cb661197b: "«component»\nEditorAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(core)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "documentChanged(document)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "documentSaved(document)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nEditorAdapter.documentChanged:\nFor the supplied editor change, capture a new SourceDocument from document.uri.toString() and document.getText() at this call. Pass that snapshot to core.preview once and return core's tabs unchanged. Preserve the full URI for file, untitled and remote documents; do not read files or request a save. Later edits must not change an earlier snapshot.\n\nEditorAdapter.documentSaved:\nFor the supplied save notification, capture a new SourceDocument from document.uri.toString() and document.getText() at this call. Pass that snapshot to core.sourceSaved once without requesting a preview or another save. Core owns the generation policy.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIxZGRiODAwMi0yYTViLTQxZjktODQ1Zi0yMWU5YjA3N2E4MDgiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkdlbmVyYXRpb25Ib3N0IiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_4f88d4f362e4313369358352dc5dcbae4c8fa2db8ca7a6cddea1b070a9de2f09: "«component»\nGenerationHost" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(context, worker)": ""
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjM1ZjdjNWRjLTczNjUtNDYyZi04YjcxLTljNDQ1Yzc0OTVkZSIsIm93bmVyIjoic180Zjg4ZDRmMzYyZTQzMTMzNjkzNTgzNTJkYzVkY2JhZTRjOGZhMmRiOGNhN2E2Y2RkZWExYjA3MGE5ZGUyZjA5IiwibmFtZSI6InN0YXJ0IiwicGFyYW1ldGVycyI6W119
  "start()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjVlNjVjNDBjLTMxMjYtNDRlNS1iZjFlLWY1MGIwY2M2M2JlNCIsIm93bmVyIjoic180Zjg4ZDRmMzYyZTQzMTMzNjkzNTgzNTJkYzVkY2JhZTRjOGZhMmRiOGNhN2E2Y2RkZWExYjA3MGE5ZGUyZjA5IiwibmFtZSI6ImJ1ZmZlcnMiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "buffers()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "present(state)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "record(configurationFile, result)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "shutdown(completion)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjgzMTcyNThjLTY2MWMtNGRhNy1hZTkwLWNmMjQzY2YzMDYzZCIsIm93bmVyIjoic180Zjg4ZDRmMzYyZTQzMTMzNjkzNTgzNTJkYzVkY2JhZTRjOGZhMmRiOGNhN2E2Y2RkZWExYjA3MGE5ZGUyZjA5IiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nGenerationHost.start:\nRegister once the real post-save and open/change/close events, Enable Generation on Save (expec.enableGenerationOnSave) and Disable Generation on Save (expec.disableGenerationOnSave). Capture URI/text/version directly from ordinary local .expec save events and forward sourceSaved without saving again. Other documents only update buffer facts. Commands adapt an explicit author choice for the selected manifest; retain its boolean in workspace state keyed by exact manifest URI, default false. Assemble one core coordinator with this native buffer/presentation adapter and supplied worker. No native parsing, generation policy or output planning. Package the owned generation-worker entry with the pinned SDK. Supply resource-scoped expec.nodeExecutable (default node; explicit path allowed) to the concrete NodeGenerationWorker with its packaged entry. Launch without a shell, never fork's default Electron executable. Show the actual child version or launch error; preview packaging alone does not prove full CLI resource closure.\n\nGenerationHost.configurationChanged:\nReceive the actual active saved ConnectionConfiguration through the selected sidebar's ConnectionWorkFeedback observer, or absence on explicit session-only disconnect, deletion, unavailable selection or transition. Authored previews and live package analysis independently retain the raw selected saved configuration; generation is no longer routed through that preview callback. Withdraw old admission and clear queued save intents before switching or suspension, while continuing to record actual terminal results and partial receipts. Load and retain only the manifest's prior explicit opt-in, never erase or grant it because of generic absence, disconnect or reconnection. A previously disabled manifest stays disabled; restoring an earlier true opt-in still needs a later genuine source save. Dirty configuration events retain saved text and notify core of actual buffer changes. Restart may replay active configuration and current buffer facts, never previous save intents. Do not edit the language manifest or infer enabled from writable/connected.\n\nGenerationHost.buffers:\nSnapshot every current workspace.textDocuments ordinary file buffer, including hidden target buffers of other languages, using its actual uri/version/getText/isDirty. Closed buffers are absent. Keep native document object/lifetime checks around delayed callbacks; never provide a cached empty or clean set. Core decides which roots/inputs these facts protect.\n\nGenerationHost.present:\nShow core's current generation status and actual explanation in one owned native status-bar item and its .expec Generation output channel. Keep this distinct from the connection directory status. Do not reinterpret permission, hide a partial-write warning or show a superseded success as current.\n\nGenerationHost.record:\nAppend the actual observed child runtime version and unchanged CLI JSON or launch/transport/cleanup failure to the owned output channel with its selected manifest context, including superseded or cancelled runs and partial effects. An exit code or dispatched notification alone is not proof of saved output.\n\nGenerationHost.shutdown:\nInvalidate save/configuration callbacks and remove owned events/commands, then dispose core and request worker shutdown. Keep terminal effect recording and its output channel alive until worker completion; then dispose remaining status/output resources, attempt all cleanup and notify this completion with any actual causes. Repeated callers join the same shutdown. The native entry wraps this callback in its one awaited Promise, preserving cleanup failures.\n\nGenerationHost.dispose:\nInitiate this same shutdown once, retaining asynchronous failure evidence. The entry point explicitly awaits shutdown completion; this native Disposable method alone is not proof of process termination. Never roll back user edits.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiIzNmFjMmEzOC02MWRlLTRkOGMtYjE5Mi01NTA0ZTM4MzFkYjYiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZURlZmluaXRpb25BZGFwdGVyIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_e864eb12b474327aeaf2574dd4e89fd537e407804353617e0cc93885b5a50943: "«component»\nSourceDefinitionAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(navigation)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "definition(document, position)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceDefinitionAdapter.definition:\nTranslate a standard LSP UTF-16 position using this exact current TextDocument text into a zero-based Unicode-scalar offset, and ask core SourceNavigation.definition once with its exact URI/version. Reject noninteger, negative or out-of-line positions with absence; do not clamp them or split a surrogate pair into a guessed scalar. Translate the returned authored name range back to standard UTF-16 Location using the reply's exact captured target text and URI. Absence stays absence. This adapter owns only coordinate/protocol conversion; it never parses, resolves, compiles, chooses a declaration, reads files, saves or generates. The shared LanguageServerAdapter owns its one registration and current document lifecycle; no second DocumentAnalysis is constructed.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI4YjJjMTlhYS04MWM3LTQyOWUtYTBlYi05YzJlMDA1YjZhMWEiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZUhvdmVyQWRhcHRlciIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_4eabae0969da9c5ab193d5ddd7669fdd77e79781766895bf979c55ae2fdb5450: "«component»\nSourceHoverAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(hover)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "information(document, position)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceHoverAdapter.information:\nConvert the exact current standard LSP TextDocument and UTF-16 Position to one SourceHover.hover query using its URI/version and a Unicode-scalar offset. Reject negative, fractional, out-of-line positions or positions inside a surrogate pair with absence; never clamp. Convert the reply's referring name range with its exact captured source back to a standard LSP Hover range. Render the authored signature in an expec fenced code block and its nonempty description as literal Markdown text beneath it. Choose a fence longer than any run of backticks in the signature, escape Markdown and HTML in the description, and never enable command links or trusted HTML. Absence stays absence. The adapter owns coordinates and presentation only; it never parses, checks, chooses a declaration, reads files, generates or constructs another analysis.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJlNzhkNmI4Mi01MTZiLTRjZDgtYWM0Mi02NGQ2NzYyMzcwYmMiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZUNvbXBsZXRpb25BZGFwdGVyIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_7c18b244f30bdb7377e911b4bf6a1136454468f02f654db62b0652db8dad559f: "«component»\nSourceCompletionAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(completion)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "items(document, position)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceCompletionAdapter.items:\nConvert this exact standard LSP TextDocument and zero-based UTF-16 Position to one current SourceCompletion query. Invalid, fractional, negative, out-of-line or surrogate-interior positions give an empty list, never a clamped query. Require the reply's captured URI/text to match this document exactly and a finite single-line range containing this requested position. Return standard plain-text CompletionItems labelled by eligible spelling with an exact TextEdit for only the captured final token, using the SDK insertionText unchanged and actual targetName as plain detail. No inferred implementation or validity, snippets, command, additionalTextEdits, resolve handler, trusted Markdown or generated edits. Absence stays an empty list. This adapter owns coordinates and presentation, not scope, parsing, resolution, acquisition, generation or file mutation.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJhNjhlYTM0Zi01MDk5LTQ1ODAtOGUyZC0wMDVhNGY1M2YzMTYiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZVJlZmVyZW5jZUFkYXB0ZXIiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_3c2b41ed4f8102edf6293aee3a4eca0c281845cbaf3295235d4f9008ce7c9380: "«component»\nSourceReferenceAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(references)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "references(document, position, includeDeclaration)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceReferenceAdapter.references:\nTranslate this exact current standard TextDocument and LSP UTF-16 position to a Unicode-scalar cursor and call SourceReferences.search once with its URI/version and unchanged includeDeclaration flag. Invalid negative, fractional, out-of-line or surrogate-splitting positions return absence without clamping. Absent core results stay absent. Require the reply's requesting URI/text to equal this document. Validate each actual occurrence's finite nonempty scalar range against its supplied captured source before converting it to standard Location; do not guess from spelling, basename or saved files. Invalid replies return absence rather than a partial fabricated success. Preserve the core's ordered distinct locations and plain coverage/prerequisite lists. This adapter performs only protocol/coordinate conversion, never parsing, resolution, compilation, acquisition, scanning, saving or generation. LanguageServerAdapter owns one standard registration and the shared analysis lifetime.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI1NzJlNDUzYy0yMjJhLTQyYjUtOTgxMS03MjAwZjhlNjllNTUiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IlNvdXJjZVJlbmFtZUFkYXB0ZXIiLCJwcm9taXNlVG9vbHRpcCI6dHJ1ZX0
s_b123b482f155911b4e2bf3caab8cd95695f3c3760bb98c9b079905d2e03448b1: "«component»\nSourceRenameAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(renamer)": ""
  # expec-uml: 
  "prepare(document, position)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "rename(document, position, newName)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nSourceRenameAdapter.prepare:\nConvert this exact standard TextDocument's UTF-16 position to a zero-based Unicode-scalar cursor and call core prepare once with the exact URI/version. Reject fractional, negative, out-of-line and surrogate-splitting coordinates rather than clamp. Validate the returned whole authored token against this same captured requesting text before returning the standard prepareRename range/decoded placeholder. Map an explained core refusal to standard LSP RequestFailed, without invented partial success. Native types and coordinate conversion stay here; no source acquisition, parsing, name policy, generation or writes.\n\nSourceRenameAdapter.rename:\nConvert the current standard document/position once and forward decoded newName unchanged to core rename. Validate all returned exact source/scalar ranges, nonoverlap, distinct document URIs and nonnegative integer optional versions, and requester URI/text/version equality when affected, before producing standard WorkspaceEdit.documentChanges with versioned TextDocumentEdits; saved-only sources have null version. Invalid results refuse the whole edit, never silently filter occurrences or guess saved versions. Preserve actual URI/text/newText and edit ordering. No custom apply, save, selection, parser, resolver or generated output. Standard VS Code owns preview/apply and undo; null-version edits and later preview selection carry no invented atomicity guarantee. Core/provider errors remain observable as explained standard refusal.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI3MDUwOGNiNy01N2FmLTQ3NDAtODc2NS1jYmYzZTY1OGQxNzQiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6Ikxhbmd1YWdlU2VydmVyQWRhcHRlciIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_5614201455f9166e7220b9b8d5d5a4b3372ca67d94bd454446eadd9d79ceb25d: "«component»\nLanguageServerAdapter" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(connection, sources, identities)": ""
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImZjYWZmZDM4LTNmZGUtNGFlNi1iNzZkLTE1ZGJkZWMxN2UwNSIsIm93bmVyIjoic181NjE0MjAxNDU1ZjkxNjZlNzIyMGI5YjhkNWQ1YTRiMzM3MmNhNjdkOTRiZDQ1NDQ0NmVhZGQ5ZDc5Y2ViMjVkIiwibmFtZSI6InN0YXJ0IiwicGFyYW1ldGVycyI6W119
  "start()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "publish(source, version, report)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "clear(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjVhOWE4Yzk2LTVjMGMtNDAxOC04MTJmLTk5OWU1ZGJkM2U5NyIsIm93bmVyIjoic181NjE0MjAxNDU1ZjkxNjZlNzIyMGI5YjhkNWQ1YTRiMzM3MmNhNjdkOTRiZDQ1NDQ0NmVhZGQ5ZDc5Y2ViMjVkIiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nLanguageServerAdapter.start:\nRegister native LSP initialization and document events once, using TextDocuments to reconstruct incremental text. Feed actual open/change/close snapshots and versions to core DocumentAnalysis. Opening must check exactly once despite TextDocuments also emitting a content-change event. Core owns checking and version/lifetime policy; this adapter owns protocol registration and translation. Register standard LSP document diagnostic pull with inter-file dependencies and no workspace diagnostic enumeration, and negotiate UTF-16 positions. Register standard LSP watched-file notifications for requested dependency URIs, including currently missing files, using native relative-pattern registration. Core chooses relevant invalidation; forward creation/change/deletion to sourceChanged. Reconcile capture-to-watch gaps by rechecking after each newly established registration. Retain registrations only for dependency URIs requested by current open entries, and dispose them when unneeded or on shutdown. Unsupported native watch capabilities remain an observable limitation rather than a promised live update. Do not scan or compile in the adapter. Register native preview selection/configuration notifications and forward them to one core OutputPreviews instance using its default shipped registrations. Its feedback emits only plain PreviewPublication values through the native channel. Do not construct another reader/compiler or inspect output models. Advertise definitionProvider and register standard textDocument/definition once. Obtain the current TextDocuments snapshot, then delegate coordinate conversion and the query to SourceDefinitionAdapter with one core SourceNavigation. Missing/cancelled/currently unavailable documents return no location. The adapter never chooses targets or rechecks source. Advertise hoverProvider and register standard textDocument/hover once. Obtain the current TextDocuments snapshot and delegate to SourceHoverAdapter using one core SourceHover; missing, cancelled or unavailable snapshots return absence. Hover uses the same existing analysis publications as diagnostics and navigation, without another reader/compiler.\nAdvertise documentSymbolProvider and register standard textDocument/documentSymbol once. Use the existing current TextDocuments snapshot and delegate to one SourceOutlineAdapter with one core DocumentOutline. Missing, cancelled, disposed or currently unavailable documents have no outline. Preserve one shared DocumentAnalysis and its current source/version/lifetime; no extra analysis, declaration walk or project connection is created for this request.\nAdvertise completionProvider without trigger characters or resolve support and register standard textDocument/completion once. Use the actual current TextDocuments entry and delegate to one SourceCompletionAdapter with one core SourceCompletion. Cancelled, missing or disposed requests return an empty list. Reuse the same existing DocumentAnalysis publication; do not parse, resolve, acquire, generate or construct a second analysis for completion.\nCapture each existing saved preview-configuration notification's exact file/text/writable scalars or absence and advance an owned latest-notification identity. Forward that captured snapshot first to the same OutputPreviews.configurationChanged to invalidate old preview work and prepare selection/options, then to the same DocumentAnalysis.configurationChanged so its new reports drive that configuration. Recheck the notification identity and adapter lifetime between forwards: a synchronous newer notification or disposal from preview feedback prevents the older snapshot from restoring package facts. Preserve currentness after reentrant analysis/feedback as well. Keep selection withdrawal and saved-text behavior; native callback exceptions remain observable. Never validate JSON in this adapter or wait for a connected target before supplying authored package facts. Configuration changes refresh current semantic reports at unchanged editor versions through the one existing analysis; no second reader/compiler, native package inspection, installation, project capture, file scan or new report identity field is introduced.\nAdvertise referencesProvider and register standard textDocument/references once. Use the current TextDocuments snapshot and delegate to one SourceReferenceAdapter with one core SourceReferences, preserving context.includeDeclaration. Missing, cancelled, disposed or currently unavailable documents return no locations. A successful presentation returns only its standard Location list through LSP. Keep its captured coverage as a point-in-time snapshot with this request lifetime, exact native analysis resultId and URI/version. Through standard connection.window.showInformationMessage display 'Reference search covers captured sources only; workspace importers were not scanned.' with a 'Show coverage' action, without delaying the Location response until a user chooses. When that choice settles, recheck the same document lifetime/version, analysis resultId, request cancellation, disposal and latest search before presenting a second standard information message listing the actual coveredUris and prerequisite entries. Entry version alone cannot identify a replacement import report; stale/superseded choices do nothing. Keep native request failures observable. No custom coverage protocol, QuickPick API, Inspection, NodeId or compiler model crosses transport. This search covers only the requester and reachable captured imports/includes, never reverse workspace importers or an undiscovered workspace.\nRegister exactly one standard prepareRename/rename handler and advertise renameProvider with prepareProvider only when the client supports WorkspaceEdit.documentChanges. Supply one core SourceRename with the existing DocumentSources, the explicitly injected SourceIdentities port, and a RenameWorkspace port adapting this server lifetime: current selected saved configuration notifications and current TextDocuments open .expec URI/text/version facts. Do not substitute unsaved JSON proposals or infer rename permission from metadata writable. Neither a connected generated-output target nor generation is required. The adapter never enumerates folders or composes models. Translate actual prepare/rename replies through SourceRenameAdapter; core owns all configured-entry acquisition, naming, collision, completeness and refusal policy. Refuse unsupported versioned-edit capability with an explanation instead of returning unversioned edits. Capture request document identity/version and configuration revision; suppress cancelled, superseded, closed or disposed responses. Dispose owned registrations once and keep errors observable. Existing diagnostics, previews, definition, hover, outline, completion and references retain their contracts.\n\nLanguageServerAdapter.publish:\nPreserve current scope findings separately from source diagnostics. Show actual dependencyProblems through standard visible LSP window warnings, including code/message and the selected manifest or supplied-mapping JSON-path origin. Do not invent source ranges for dependency origins or mutate Compilation. Deduplicate unchanged warnings for the same current saved configuration/finding so ordinary typing cannot flood notifications; changed, invalid or withdrawn configuration must not reuse an old warning as current evidence. The same current report still reaches previews before native projection.\nRetain real syntax and compiler errors whose primary source URI matches this document in its current native pull cache. Foreign primary findings remain in the raw Compilation and output log; an open imported document receives its own entry analysis. Never attach a foreign primary range to the requesting document. Convert each scalar range with the captured text for that range's exact URI, including cross-file related information. Preserve messages and codes. Keep nonlocated problems and deferred requirements observable in the language-client output log without inventing editor positions. Replace old feedback, including an empty full report when findings clear. Give each accepted publication an opaque analysis resultId; editor version alone cannot identify changed imports. Request the SDK diagnostic refresh after dependent feedback changes. Never reparse, generate or make semantic decisions here. Forward this same captured source/version/report to core OutputPreviews before reducing it to native diagnostic data; preserve ordinary diagnostic publication and dependency-watch behavior. Forward this same current source/version/report to one core SourceNavigation before native conversion. Forward this same current source/version/report to one core SourceHover before native conversion, including same-version replacement reports after imported edits. No Inspection or Specification crosses the protocol boundary.\nForward the same current captured source/version/report to DocumentOutline before answering native symbol requests. A replacement or rejected report replaces its earlier tree even at the same editor version; transport only plain native symbols, never Inspection or a compiler model.\nForward this same current captured source/version/report to SourceCompletion before native conversion, including same-version replacement after imported edits and rejected reports that withdraw old completion facts. Transport only plain native CompletionItems; Inspection and Resolution stay within core.\nForward this same current captured source/version/report to SourceReferences before native reference conversion, including same-version dependency replacements and rejected reports. Do not create another reader, resolver, compiler, file scan or reference model.\n\nLanguageServerAdapter.clear:\nRemove the closed document from the pull-response cache. Native document diagnostic pull owns editor close cleanup; never resurrect a cached response from an earlier lifetime. Forward this closed URI to core OutputPreviews so pending work and selected content from the closed lifetime are withdrawn. End the same core SourceNavigation and SourceHover report lifetimes through closed(uri).\nEnd this same DocumentOutline lifetime through closed(uri); later requests cannot use the closed document's tree.\nEnd this same SourceCompletion lifetime through closed(uri); later completion requests cannot use its earlier facts.\nEnd this same SourceReferences lifetime through closed(uri) and invalidate later coverage actions from that closed lifetime. A visible summary is a historical snapshot, not a claim of current coverage.\n\nLanguageServerAdapter.dispose:\nRemove owned subscriptions, end tracked document lifetimes and prevent further diagnostic publication. Repeated disposal is harmless. Leave connection/process shutdown to the native server entry point. Dispose core OutputPreviews, invalidating pending output work; started renderer callbacks retain their own asynchronous cleanup obligation. Dispose SourceNavigation and its retained reports; later definition requests cannot use old targets. Dispose SourceHover; later hover requests cannot retain earlier meaning.\nRelease the owned document-symbol registration once and dispose DocumentOutline. Later callbacks cannot publish or return a retained tree.\nRelease the owned completion registration once and dispose SourceCompletion. Later callbacks cannot publish or return retained suggestions.\nRelease the owned reference registration and invalidate owned asynchronous coverage choices once, dispose SourceReferences and prevent later callbacks from returning old matches or presenting retained coverage.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJkNjFlZGQ3ZC05YWZhLTQ0YjMtODEyMy01YzdiODdjZDMwODQiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkZpbGVTb3VyY2VzIiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_7b58d9f9fcf658a8bdc74ace8c3a623f475e9515eecd931be24568fca276336f: "«component»\nFileSources" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "read(uri)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "localPath(uri, manifestFile)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "keyOf(uri, manifestFile)": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nFileSources.read:\nAdapt a local file URI to its current UTF-8 saved text for DocumentSources. Missing files and unsupported URI schemes return absence. Other filesystem errors surface. Do not scan folders, acquire packages, cache business state or replace open editor text.\n\nFileSources.localPath:\nAdapt the exact file URI and selected absolute manifest filename into a verified primary manifest-directory-relative path through native path/ancestry identity APIs. Use portable / separators, preserve literal case/name, and never derive ownership by textual URI-prefix subtraction or from a generated target. Verify existing root/ancestors and ordinary file routes; a named unsaved file may use a verified existing parent without reading, creating or requiring its contents. Reject symlink escapes and alias routes that cannot establish the same source identity; unavailable or outside-root routes and nonfile/untitled URIs have no local path. A nested build.sourceRoots does not replace the primary root; an additional outside root cannot gain a guessed folder scope. Other filesystem errors surface. Core caches/invalidate these supplied facts; this native adapter adds no scope policy, configuration parser, whole-project discovery, installation or writes.\n\nFileSources.keyOf:\nSupply SourceIdentities from verified native physical file facts under this selected primary manifest root. For an existing ordinary file, return an opaque key whose equality identifies the same physical file through supported drive/URI spellings, filename-case aliases or hardlinks; distinct physical files remain distinct even on a case-sensitive filesystem. Verify root/ancestors and the source identity before and after acquisition, reject unsupported identities, escaping/symlink routes and changed facts, and keep unexpected filesystem errors observable. A never-saved named file or unavailable/unprovable physical identity has no key; create nothing and allow the rename caller to explain that saving is needed. Do not derive identity from URI text, path case folding, canonical pathname alone, source contents or a global cache. Preserve localPath's literal scoped-path semantics. The key is comparable only within this manifest/request and its final recheck, never a durable ID or transport value. No folder scan, parser, project capture, installation, save or generation.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiJmZjkzNzM3NS1lZWRhLTQ1NTYtYTZhNC1kOTY3NGRmMWM1YzIiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6IkVkaXRvckxhbmd1YWdlU3VwcG9ydCIsInByb21pc2VUb29sdGlwIjp0cnVlfQ
s_9a5eb514b396ae71740452b876c21d0424c6ffb5f27357d723ada2d1c9d53026: "«component»\nEditorLanguageSupport" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(context, client)": ""
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImMzMmQ2MjNkLWQ0YTQtNDBjMC05YTViLWVmNDU4OGUxNjE1ZiIsIm93bmVyIjoic185YTVlYjUxNGIzOTZhZTcxNzQwNDUyYjg3NmMyMWQwNDI0YzZmZmI1ZjI3MzU3ZDcyM2FkYTJkMWM5ZDUzMDI2IiwibmFtZSI6InN0YXJ0IiwicGFyYW1ldGVycyI6W119
  "start()": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6ImNlN2VjNDkwLWUzMjYtNGRmYi1hOWJiLWQwODZiYTM5MDBmZCIsIm93bmVyIjoic185YTVlYjUxNGIzOTZhZTcxNzQwNDUyYjg3NmMyMWQwNDI0YzZmZmI1ZjI3MzU3ZDcyM2FkYTJkMWM5ZDUzMDI2IiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nEditorLanguageSupport.start:\nRequest startup of the supplied native LanguageClient once. The native entry point owns its construction, packaged TypeScript server, expec selector (file and untitled), and single awaited stop on deactivation. Return that native client through the standard VS Code activation export for callers of its native feature APIs. Register owned resources with this extension context. Use native document diagnostic pull on edits. In the public provideDiagnostics middleware capture native document identity/version before awaiting next, then cancel an obsolete/closed result instead of returning empty success. The SDK owns scheduling, cancellation and diagnostic collections. Never replace newer feedback or reopen diagnostics for a closed document; do not rely on push version fields. Guard public provideDefinition middleware with the requesting native document identity/version around its await, preserving prior middleware. Cancel obsolete, closed, disposed or cancelled requests rather than returning an old target. For returned target URIs already open when the request began, also refuse a result if that captured target buffer changed or ended its lifetime while awaiting. Core reports establish point-in-time meaning; this does not promise editor/filesystem atomicity across the process boundary. Guard public provideHover middleware with requesting native document identity/version around its await, preserving prior middleware. Capture the requesting document and currently open expec buffer identities/versions before awaiting. After the prior middleware or next resolves, cancel if disposed, token-cancelled, or any captured buffer changed, closed or was replaced, since a hover reply does not identify its declaration source across the native boundary. Restore only this adapter's own middleware on disposal. This conservative pending-request guard does not claim filesystem/editor atomicity or replace core resolution policy. Keep startup failures observable and keep core policy out of this host adapter.\nGuard standard provideDocumentSymbols middleware with the requesting native document identity/version around awaiting next. Preserve prior middleware and restore only the wrapper this adapter owns. Cancel an obsolete, closed, disposed or cancelled response rather than returning an old outline or invented empty success. Other unchanged documents remain usable. The native SDK owns the outline UI and scheduling; this adapter owns only native request currentness.\nGuard the public provideCompletionItem middleware around awaiting the prior middleware or real continuation, preserving its exact replies. Capture the requesting document identity/version and currently open expec buffer identities/versions. Cancel a pending reply after requester or captured import-buffer change, close or replacement, token cancellation or disposal. Other-language buffer changes do not cancel completion. Release only this adapter's own wrapper. This protects a pending response; it does not promise editor/filesystem atomicity or safety when a user later chooses an already returned item. Core owns candidate policy and prepared facts.\nGuard standard provideReferences middleware around awaiting its prior middleware or next, preserving the actual includeDeclaration context and returned locations. Capture the requesting document and all currently open expec buffer identities/versions; cancel if the requester or any captured buffer changed, closed or was replaced, or if disposed/token-cancelled. Preserve prior middleware and restore only this wrapper on disposal. The native LanguageClient handles standard server ShowMessageRequests for the visible bounded coverage summary/action; no separate coverage channel or business model is added here. Native SDK owns reference navigation and selection. This is a point-in-time report, not editor/filesystem atomicity; no native scans, saves or generation are added.\nGuard the standard prepareRename and provideRenameEdits middleware around awaiting the previous middleware or real continuation. Preserve decoded newName and the exact native result; capture requesting document identity/version plus all currently open .expec buffer identities/versions. Cancel if a captured buffer changes, closes or is replaced, the request token is cancelled, the selected configuration notification revision changes, or this adapter is disposed. Restore only owned wrappers and preserve prior middleware. Standard VS Code owns rename input, preview/apply, optional preview selection and undo; never write files or claim atomicity after a returned response. No duplicate native edit application or generated-output invocation.\n\nEditorLanguageSupport.dispose:\nInvalidate adapter-owned callbacks and remove owned registrations once. The native entry point owns the injected client and awaits its one stop promise on deactivation; this operation neither stops that client twice nor promises synchronous process termination.\n```"
}
# expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsImRlZmluaXRpb24iOiI1YmMxYjU3Yi03NGUwLTRhN2UtYWY0MS0yZWM2YWU0ZDgxY2UiLCJraW5kIjoiY29tcG9uZW50IiwibmFtZSI6Ik91dHB1dFByZXZpZXdIb3N0IiwicHJvbWlzZVRvb2x0aXAiOnRydWV9
s_3fee3d54dfbefd357cc01c0398d2b02b47c85363a8459073be41a33be54171c9: "«component»\nOutputPreviewHost" {
  shape: class
  # expec-uml: 
  "construction(context, client)": ""
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjY1ZjlkOTc2LWYwMmUtNGE4My1hNDM4LTk4ZDFhNDFiNDRjZiIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZmVlM2Q1NGRmYmVmZDM1N2NjMDFjMDM5OGQyYjAyYjQ3Yzg1MzYzYTg0NTkwNzNiZTQxYTMzYmU1NDE3MWM5IiwibmFtZSI6InN0YXJ0IiwicGFyYW1ldGVycyI6W119
  "start()": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "configurationChanged(configuration)": "..."
  # expec-uml: 
  "present(publication)": "..."
  # expec-uml: eyJmb3JtYXQiOjEsIm91dHB1dElkIjoidW1sIiwidmlldyI6InN0cnVjdHVyZSIsIm1lbWJlciI6IjBmNzM1NDAxLWIwNTUtNDVmMi05MjUzLWJjZDQ0MWVkOTViZSIsIm93bmVyIjoic18zZmVlM2Q1NGRmYmVmZDM1N2NjMDFjMDM5OGQyYjAyYjQ3Yzg1MzYzYTg0NTkwNzNiZTQxYTMzYmU1NDE3MWM5IiwibmFtZSI6ImRpc3Bvc2UiLCJwYXJhbWV0ZXJzIjpbXX0
  "dispose()": "..."
  tooltip: "```text\nOutputPreviewHost.start:\nRegister Show Output Previews (expec.showOutputPreviews), the client notification handler and native editor-selection events once. Starting or activating the adapter registers the command without opening a panel. Invoking Show Output Previews creates or reveals one ordinary VS Code webview panel containing the packaged React OutputTabs application. Its browser bootstrap mounts OutputTabs and uses the existing Vite/React build to bundle React and ReactDOM locally, not external runtime imports. Package the resulting script/style assets under dist/webview in the VSIX. Preserve the real shipped UML renderer SDK worker and WASM runtime, including its module-relative resources and paths, so packaged native server rendering works without a checkout or external runtime download. Browser asset build and native renderer resource packaging precede implementation testing. Follow the current expec editor URI, including untitled; focusing the panel retains the last authored selection. Forward selection to server core without reading or compiling documents. Subscribe before client startup and replay latest selected URI and saved configuration when the same client becomes running, including restart. The existing native client and diagnostic feature APIs remain intact. Register owned resources in the supplied context; host lifetime guards only prevent disposed callbacks, not another business revision engine.\n\nOutputPreviewHost.configurationChanged:\nForward this captured saved configuration snapshot, or selection absence, to server core through the native client. Buffer the latest snapshot until the client is running. Do not parse or validate it, infer target readiness, capture project code, install packages or generate. Dirty configuration behavior is supplied by ConnectionSidebar and remains saved-text behavior.\n\nOutputPreviewHost.present:\nAdapt one current plain core presentation to the webview message channel. Cache only the latest full presentation for ready replay, panel recreation and temporarily hidden panels; postMessage success is dispatch only, not proof of rendering. Never transport Specification, compiler models, functions or private ownership data. Set webview HTML once per lifetime, mount the bundled React application before ready, and replay to that exact live panel. Resolve only packaged local script/style assets with asWebviewUri and restrict localResourceRoots to their folder. Enable scripts only; disable forms and command URIs. Use a CSP beginning default-src none with only the bundled scripts/styles and required inert data images allowed. Literal text is never HTML and SVG is never injected inline or fetched from target paths. Present the core source context and whole-view explanation as well as its ordered tabs.\n\nOutputPreviewHost.dispose:\nDispose every owned panel, command and event/message subscription, attempt all cleanup even if one resource fails, and prevent later dispatch or selection/configuration events. Panel closure releases its webview only and does not stop language analysis; reopening receives the latest current presentation. The native entry point owns the supplied client and its one awaited stop.\n```"
}
